The applicant is based in Maryland, US. Only include funders that accept applicants from there; skip programs restricted to other countries or regions. Work out for yourself the kinds of investors that fit (by stage, cheque size, sector thesis and geography) and search each kind with several differently worded queries. Prefer each investor's own website (thesis, portfolio and team pages) and recent deal announcements from 2025-2026; do not rely on lists or rankings alone. For every investor give: name, official URL of its own thesis or portfolio page, stage and typical cheque size as stated, evidence of a deal in the last 18 months (with date), how to pitch (form, email or warm intro), why it fits, red flags, and a short literal quote from its page that supports the thesis fit. Finish with the investors you excluded and why.'...
